            "twitter": ""
          }
        ],
        "abstract": "Autosar guidelines for the use of the C++14 language in critical and safety-related systems propose rules that are tailored to improve security, safety and quality of software. In this talk, we will discuss main challenges in extending Clang with source code analyses that are necessary for checking compliance of software with Autosar automotive standard: We will present Clang’s current support for checking compliance to different standards and its strengths and weakness in this area We will compare efficiency and possibilities based on implementing analyses via AST Visitors and AST Matchers. We will present our improvements of Clang's diagnostics. We will discuss similarities and differences between our approach and the solution offered by Clang-Tidy project. We will present some impressions and results on using our extension of Clang (supporting checking compliance with more than 180 Autosar rules) in automotive industry, including running it on parts of Automotive Grade Linux open source code.",
